WHY A SHARED COMPONENT
Both the payments and expenses tables need the same heading, and Phase 3 reuses
this rather than duplicating the markup. 'figures' is a ReactNode slot rather
than a typed prop because payments carry agent fees alongside gross rent while
expenses carry only a total — the shape differs, the chrome does not.

TWO LOAD-BEARING DETAILS, BOTH EASY TO UNDO BY ACCIDENT
1. position:sticky is on the th, not the tr. Sticky on a table ROW is not
   reliably supported across browsers; on a cell it is. The first draft of this
   component put it on the tr and was corrected before commit.
2. The hairlines are a box-shadow, not border-y. Tailwind's preflight sets
   border-collapse:collapse, and a collapsed border belongs to the table rather
   than the cell, so it does not travel with the cell once stuck. The shadow
   does. It draws from var(--border), which is defined for both themes in
   app/globals.css, so the divider follows the theme with no dark-mode branch.

ACCESSIBILITY
th with scope="colgroup" spanning the full column set, so a screen reader
announces the year as the heading for the rows beneath rather than reading a
stray cell.

THEMING
bg-background and var(--border) are semantic tokens with light and dark values
already defined (app/globals.css lines 64/79 light, 125/140 dark). No fixed
colours. The background must stay opaque or rows show through while scrolling.

